  "title": "protobuf: Close repeated field JSON arrays followed by unknown fields",
  "description": "Repeated fields in protobuf, when expressed in JSON, use JSON arrays.\nThe JSON array cannot be closed until we either get a different field\ntype, or end the entire parsing (possibly by aborting.) There's one\ncheck for ending the pending array if the last validly parsed field\nwas a repeated field.\n\nHowever, when a repeated field is followed by an unknown field,\ndissect_one_protobuf_field returns true, which results in\nprev_field_desc being set to the null value, and the array not\nbeing closed. Close a pending array if the new field is unknown.\n\nFix #20178.",
